# A great run on Civic Center (the score tiers' measure): UN Plaza's north row every 10 s (the teleport
# stands in for rolling back): four ledges, popped off each onto the next with a kickflip, a heelflip
# and a pop shove-it between, 11,400 (11,392 before city phase 11); eleven, 125,400. Pro (14,000) on the second, Sick (115,000) on
# the eleventh. (Before the feel audit's balance damping the bot's balance taps once made the
# shove-it a Kickflip Superman with the special meter full: 136,512, Sick on the tenth.) A decent run (two ledges, 2,376, every 20 s) scores 14,256. The row's ledges, 3.4 m apart, make
# the Tour's longest lines: about twice the other levels' best.
